`build --out <path>` writes the document to that path and prints the
path it wrote, so a caller knows where the output went without having
to guess. The file itself is checked by `build-out.out/`, which is what
pins the generated-file header: `hllc` recognizes its own output by
that header before overwriting anything, so the exact bytes at the top
of every generated file are load-bearing, not decoration.

```console
$ hllc build web.hll --out docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.yml

```
